WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:09.361
Izzie and her grandmother walked into cooking class together.

2
00:00:09.362 --> 00:00:14.847
"This will be fun, Isabel!" Grandma said.

3
00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.264
"Ugh," Izzie thought.

4
00:00:17.265 --> 00:00:20.489
"She called me Isabel again!"

5
00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.867
Izzie wanted to tell Grandma that she didn't like being called Isabel.

6
00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:29.072
But she didn't want to hurt Grandma's feelings.

7
00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:32.242
The boys were washing their hands.

8
00:00:32.243 --> 00:00:37.526
"Hi, Bobby and Jason!" Izzie said. "This is my grandma."

9
00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:41.263
"Hi," the boys said together.

10
00:00:41.264 --> 00:00:45.202
"Our friend Nina isn't here today," Jason said.

11
00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:48.501
"Her family is visiting Korea."

12
00:00:48.502 --> 00:00:53.606
"I take a senior cooking class with Chef," Grandma said.

13
00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:58.341
"I missed a class, so I'm doing a make-up with you."

14
00:00:58.342 --> 00:01:02.008
"Cool!" Bobby said.

15
00:01:02.009 --> 00:01:05.071
Chef greeted everyone.

16
00:01:05.072 --> 00:01:09.090
"Today we're making Rainbow Stir-Fry."

17
00:01:09.091 --> 00:01:12.503
Grandma looked at the recipe on the screen.

18
00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:16.027
"Why is it called 'rainbow' stir-fry?"

19
00:01:16.028 --> 00:01:20.146
"Chef says we should eat the rainbow,'" Izzie said.

20
00:01:20.147 --> 00:01:24.433
"That means eating lots of colorful fruits and vegetables.

21
00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:27.712
They're full of nutrients."

22
00:01:27.713 --> 00:01:30.652
Grandma pinched Izzie's cheeks.

23
00:01:30.653 --> 00:01:36.608
"My little granddaughter is so smart!"

24
00:01:36.609 --> 00:01:40.724
"Yikes!" Izzie whispered to the boys.

25
00:01:40.725 --> 00:01:44.487
"This is so embarrassing."

26
00:01:44.488 --> 00:01:50.325
"My grandfather treats me like a baby too," Jason whispered.

27
00:01:50.326 --> 00:01:55.883
"Last Hanukkah he gave me a huge stuffed animal."

28
00:01:55.884 --> 00:02:03.209
"Grandparents want us to stay little forever," Bobby whispered.

29
00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:06.272
Everyone got busy chopping vegetables.

30
00:02:06.273 --> 00:02:08.886
Grandma cut up red cabbage.

31
00:02:08.887 --> 00:02:12.758
Jason chopped broccoli, and Bobby cut the bell pepper.

32
00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:15.908
Izzie chopped carrots.

33
00:02:15.909 --> 00:02:19.551
Chef heated oil in a wok.

34
00:02:19.552 --> 00:02:23.663
"For stir-fries, we don't add all the vegetables at once.

35
00:02:23.664 --> 00:02:27.922
We start with those that take longest to cook."

36
00:02:27.923 --> 00:02:30.195
He looked at the class.

37
00:02:30.196 --> 00:02:32.976
"What should I cook first?"

38
00:02:32.977 --> 00:02:36.400
"Broccoli?" Bobby asked.

39
00:02:36.401 --> 00:02:39.084
"Nope," Chef said.

40
00:02:39.085 --> 00:02:43.541
"I think carrots take longer," Izzie said. "Yes!

41
00:02:43.542 --> 00:02:49.515
Carrots first, then broccoli," Chef said. "Bell

42
00:02:49.516 --> 00:02:53.182
pepper next," Bobby said. "Then

43
00:02:53.183 --> 00:02:57.159
cabbage," Jason said. Chef

44
00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.908
nodded. "Bobby, please open that can of baby corn. It

45
00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:05.937
cooks quickly, so we'll add it last." He

46
00:03:05.938 --> 00:03:11.207
turned to Izzie. "Please get the chicken from the refrigerator. Your

47
00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:17.233
grandmother can cut it into thin strips." Grandma

48
00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:28.049
chuckled. "When Isabel was little, she called the refrigerator a foodrater .

49
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:30.132
Isn't that cute?"

50
00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:35.201
"Not again!" Izzie thought as she got the chicken.

51
00:03:35.202 --> 00:03:42.086
"Another embarrassing comment!"

52
00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:47.494
While Grandma sliced the chicken, the kids began making the sauce.

53
00:03:47.495 --> 00:03:49.651
Izzie chopped ginger.

54
00:03:49.652 --> 00:03:54.022
Jason chopped garlic, and Bobby squeezed the lemon.

55
00:03:54.023 --> 00:04:01.370
They added those ingredients to vegetable oil, soy sauce, and honey.

56
00:04:01.371 --> 00:04:06.610
"I'm surprised we're making a healthy dish," Grandma said.

57
00:04:06.611 --> 00:04:12.758
"I thought we'd make something that kids like. Like hot dogs."

58
00:04:12.759 --> 00:04:18.775
"I love eating healthy foods and trying new things!" Izzie burst out.

59
00:04:18.776 --> 00:04:23.273
Grandma looked surprised. "Really?"

60
00:04:23.274 --> 00:04:26.629
"Yes!" Izzie said.

61
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:31.550
"This class is the same as my adult classes," Chef said.

62
00:04:31.551 --> 00:04:36.099
"We learn all about food," Bobby said.

63
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.533
"And how to do things ourselves," Izzie said.

64
00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:44.993
Grandma nodded but didn't say anything.

65
00:04:44.994 --> 00:04:50.356
Jason moved the cooked vegetables to a bowl.

66
00:04:50.357 --> 00:04:55.977
Izzie helped Chef stir-fry the chicken.

67
00:04:55.978 --> 00:05:00.744
When it was cooked, Bobby put the vegetables back in the wok.

68
00:05:00.745 --> 00:05:03.665
Grandma added the sauce.

69
00:05:03.666 --> 00:05:09.122
All the ingredients simmered together.

70
00:05:09.123 --> 00:05:13.169
Chef served the stir-fry over cooked rice.

71
00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:17.774
"Now we can eat!"

72
00:05:17.775 --> 00:05:22.127
"Yum!" Grandma smiled at Izzie.

73
00:05:22.128 --> 00:05:27.410
"You're growing up fast, Isabel, er . . . Izzie."

74
00:05:27.411 --> 00:05:35.059
Izzie grinned. "I'm glad you came today, Grandma."

